# Copy this to .env (docker-compose loads .env from the project root
# automatically — no `export` needed) and fill in a real value with:
#
#   python3 scripts/generate_kafka_cluster_id.py
#
# GENERATE THIS ONCE. Do not regenerate it on every `docker compose up` —
# Kafka writes this ID into kafka_data/ (the persisted volume) the first
# time the broker starts, and every startup after that checks the
# configured value still matches what's on disk. Change it later and the
# broker will refuse to start against that volume's existing data, or
# treat it as a different cluster entirely. One value, for the life of
# this cluster's data — same idea as a database's cluster/system identifier.
KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID=
